      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Venting is pointless. Honestly, if I had a choice, I would choose a future where AI never came into existence, so I wouldn’t have to face the most terrifying wave of unemployment in human history looming ahead of us. But that’s obviously wishful thinking.\n\nThe question is, how do you tell which creative works were made using AI? Maybe we can still identify most AI-generated content today, but what about in the future? OpenAI is already tearing through math problems. Mathematicians are far more alarmed than you are, but what can they actually do about it? Set up a filter to screen out AI-generated mathematical proofs?\n\nFor AI, churning out 3D virtual assets is a million times easier than solving difficult problems in mathematics or physics. It doesn’t even need specialized training—its ability to generalize is enough.\n\nInstead of burying your head in the sand like an ostrich and pretending AI-generated content doesn’t exist, you’d be better off thinking about how to build an effective AI-assisted workflow, so you don’t get left behind by everyone else.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
